---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';

// Written 2026-07-28 from the actual implementation: GA4 (G-65PEMEYW2M)
// loads ONLY after Accept on the consent banner (Consent.astro); the consent
// choice and all site preferences live in localStorage; the service worker
// caches pages for offline. No advertising cookies, nothing before consent.
const UPDATED = '28 July 2026';
---
<Base
  title="Cookie Policy | Save My Gig!"
  description="The one optional analytics cookie Save My Gig uses, what lives in your browser instead of cookies, and how to refuse or remove all of it."
  path="/legal/cookies"
  noindex
>
  <main class="wrap">
    <div class="status-line">LEGAL</div>
    <h1 style="margin-bottom:0.6rem">Cookie Policy</h1>
    <p class="dim" style="margin-bottom:2rem">Last updated: {UPDATED} · Part of <a href="/legal">the legal shelf</a></p>

    <p class="dim" style="margin-bottom:2rem">
      Short version: this site sets no cookies at all until you choose Accept on
      the banner, and the only cookies it can ever set are analytics. Decline
      and the site works exactly the same, with nothing set.
    </p>

    <div class="panel">
      <h3 style="margin-bottom:0.6rem">The one category of cookies we use</h3>
      <p class="dim">
        <strong>Analytics (optional, off by default).</strong> If you accept on
        the banner, we load Google Analytics 4 (Google LLC), which sets cookies
        beginning with <span class="mono">_ga</span>. We use it to see which
        pages actually help DJs and where people get stuck, nothing more. If you
        decline, Google Analytics is never loaded and these cookies are never
        set. Google describes its own processing in its privacy policy at
        <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" rel="noopener">policies.google.com/privacy</a>.
      </p>
      <p class="dim" style="margin-bottom:0">
        We set <strong>no advertising cookies</strong> and do
        <strong>no cross-site tracking</strong>, with or without consent.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="panel">
      <h3 style="margin-bottom:0.6rem">What lives in your browser instead</h3>
      <p class="dim">
        The site stores some data in your browser's local storage. Local storage
        is not a cookie: it never travels with your requests and is never sent
        to us or to anyone else. It holds your cookie choice itself (so the
        banner does not ask on every visit), your checklist (items, edits,
        ticks, notes), and whether registered features are unlocked on this
        device.
      </p>
      <p class="dim" style="margin-bottom:0">
        The site can also install a small offline cache (a service worker) so
        the rescue pages keep working in a basement booth with no signal. That
        cache contains our pages, nothing about you.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="panel">
      <h3 style="margin-bottom:0.6rem">Changing your mind</h3>
      <p class="dim" style="margin-bottom:0">
        Clear this site's data in your browser (cookies and site data) and
        everything above is gone: the analytics cookies, the stored choice, and
        the local data. On your next visit the banner asks again. You can also
        block cookies for this site entirely in your browser settings; the
        rescue flow does not need them.
      </p>
    </div>

    <p class="dim" style="font-size:0.85rem;margin-top:2rem">
      This policy is part of <a href="/legal">the legal shelf</a>, alongside the
      <a href="/legal/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>. Questions:
      <a href="mailto:savemygig@gmail.com">savemygig@gmail.com</a>.
    </p>
  </main>
</Base>
